MacShack Windows kit
====================

This folder is not under MacShack's MIT license (../LICENSE). It builds the Windows kit: the Windows-side pieces
MacShack Play needs for Steam, as one zip released with MacShack and downloaded by MacShack on the device. Nothing in
this folder is compiled into MacShack or MacShack Play.

Built from, each fetched at build time at the pin in pins.sh and never copied here (except NotProton's notices in
notproton/, kept as it ships them):

  NotProton (https://github.com/NotProtonNot/NotProton), v1.0.3, GPL-3.0. Its notices, as it ships them:
  notproton/NOTICE, notproton/LICENSE.lsteamclient, notproton/LICENSE.steam-shim.
  - lsteamclient: Valve's Proton lsteamclient with NotProton's files, under the Steamworks SDK license
    (notproton/LICENSE.lsteamclient). MacShack's change for Madeira, lsteamclient/macshack-unixlib.patch, is under
    the same license.
  - steam.exe: NotProton's steam-shim, a port of Proton 9's steam_helper, BSD-3-Clause
    (notproton/LICENSE.steam-shim). Built unchanged, with NotProton's own scripts. It also contains upstream Wine's
    (wine-11.15, 2df1ee28039cf84776eb1421ed90bd154cebb65f, https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine.git: the commit
    NotProton's bridge/setup-wine-tree.sh pins) winecrt0 and the static parts of its ucrtbase (LGPL-2.1-or-later,
    licenses/wine-COPYING.LIB), compiler-rt, libc++, libc++abi and libunwind (LLVM, University of Illinois/NCSA or
    MIT; licenses/wine-compiler-rt.txt, wine-libc++.txt, wine-libc++abi.txt, wine-libunwind.txt), statically linked;
    source at that commit.
  - ntdll detour: NotProton's ntdll-patch/detour.c and link64.ld, GPL-3.0, unchanged. ntdll/ (MacShack's Madeira
    variant of NotProton's shim and resolver) and the detour bytes in ntdll.patch.json are GPL-3.0 (only), as the
    NotProton code they derive from.
  Madeira's Wine (https://github.com/willfaust/wine, LGPL-2.1-or-later): its build tools, headers and import
  libraries. lsteamclient.dll also contains its winecrt0 (LGPL-2.1-or-later, licenses/madeira-wine-COPYING.LIB) and
  compiler-rt (University of Illinois/NCSA or MIT, licenses/madeira-wine-compiler-rt.txt), statically linked; source
  at that commit.
  mingw-w64 runtime (from llvm-mingw): macshack-launch.exe and steamapi-test.exe contain it, statically linked
  (licenses/mingw-w64-runtime.txt). msi.dll is built without it.
  Madeira v0.1.3's ntdll.dll (https://github.com/willfaust/Madeira, GPL-3.0-or-later): read for the detour's
  addresses; the kit carries only the detour's bytes, applied on the device.
  Madeira v0.1.3's build/madeira_cfg.h (GPL-3.0-or-later): a header Madeira's Wine includes, there only so Wine's
  build configures; none of it is in the kit.

MacShack's own files here (scripts, helpers/): GPL-3.0-or-later (LICENSE), Copyright the MacShack authors.
Valve's Steam client files are never part of the kit: the device downloads them from Valve.
